WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Roughly once every twenty-eight days,

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.610
one of a woman's
ovaries releases an egg.

3
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.530
Month after month, the cycle repeats.

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.880
Yet nothing in the body
is counting the days.

5
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.550
There's no calendar and no alarm.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.850
So how does the body keep
time without a clock?

7
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.830
In this mission, you'll
follow the menstrual cycle,

8
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.570
from the release of an
egg, called ovulation,

9
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.110
to the rebuilding of the
lining of the uterus.

10
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.810
You'll meet oestrogen, which
helps rebuild that lining.

11
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.050
And you'll meet progesterone,

12
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.950
which keeps it ready
for a fertilised egg.

13
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.900
Your mission: find out what
keeps the cycle on time.
